framework_component_specs.PillarCard:
# PillarCard

Content hub navigation card with a 16:9 image, title, description, optional child articles, and footer CTA.

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `href` | `string` | Required | Pillar page URL |
| `title` | `string` | Required | Pillar title |
| `description` | `string` | Required | Pillar description |
| `heading` | `string` | — | Small heading above title |
| `image` | `string` | — | Image URL |
| `imageAlt` | `string` | `title` | Image alt text |
| `fallbackImage` | `string` | — | Image used after loading fails |
| `childLinks` | `ChildLink[]` | — | Related articles |
| `maxChildren` | `number` | `3` | Maximum children shown |
| `ctaLabel` | `string` | `"View all"` | Footer text |
| `ctaHref` | `string` | `href` | Footer destination |
| `priority` | `boolean` | `false` | Eager, high-priority image loading |
| `className` | `string` | — | Additional container classes |

## Semantic hints
`pillar`, `category`, `topic-card`, `section-card`, `hub-card`, `collection-card`, `category-card`

## Behavior and presentation
Use for pillars/categories and related articles on hub pages. Use React Router `Link` for internal navigation. Keep the article container separate from links to avoid nested anchors. Render a linked `h3`; place cards beneath an appropriate page heading. Give child “View” links descriptive accessible names.

Use a white, rounded card with subtle border/shadow, hover elevation, muted clamped description, compact child rows, and full-width footer. Tailwind classes below are implementation choices, not established project tokens.

## Working example — `app/articles/PillarCard.tsx`

```tsx
import { Link } from "react-router";

type ChildLink = {
  title: string;
  href: string;
  description?: string;
};

type PillarCardProps = {
  href: string;
  title: string;
  description: string;
  heading?: string;
  image?: string;
  imageAlt?: string;
  fallbackImage?: string;
  childLinks?: ChildLink[];
  maxChildren?: number;
  ctaLabel?: string;
  ctaHref?: string;
  priority?: boolean;
  className?: string;
};

export function PillarCard({
  href, title, description, heading, image, imageAlt = title,
  fallbackImage, childLinks = [], maxChildren = 3,
  ctaLabel = "View all", ctaHref = href, priority = false,
  className = "",
}: PillarCardProps) {
  return (
    <article className={`overflow-hidden rounded-lg border bg-white shadow-sm hover:shadow-md ${className}`}>
      {image && (
        <Link to={href}>
          <img
            className="aspect-video w-full object-cover"
            src={image}
            alt={imageAlt}
            loading={priority ? "eager" : "lazy"}
            fetchPriority={priority ? "high" : "auto"}
            onError={(event) => {
              const target = event.currentTarget;
              if (fallbackImage && target.getAttribute("src") !== fallbackImage) {
                target.src = fallbackImage;
              }
            }}
          />
        </Link>
      )}
      <div className="p-4">
        {heading && <span>{heading}</span>}
        <h3 className="font-bold"><Link to={href}>{title}</Link></h3>
        <p className="line-clamp-3 text-gray-600">{description}</p>
        {childLinks.length > 0 && (
          <ul>
            {childLinks.slice(0, Math.max(0, maxChildren)).map((child) => (
              <li key={child.href} className="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 py-2">
                <div>
                  <span>{child.title}</span>
                  {child.description && <p>{child.description}</p>}
                </div>
                <Link to={child.href} aria-label={`View ${child.title}`}>View</Link>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )}
      </div>
      <Link to={ctaHref} className="block bg-gray-50 p-4">
        {ctaLabel} <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </Link>
    </article>
  );
}
```

Render inside a React Router route:

```tsx
<PillarCard
  href="/pillars/ai-fundamentals"
  title="AI Fundamentals"
  description="Learn AI basics."
  image="/images/ai-fundamentals.jpg"
  childLinks={[
    { title: "Machine Learning", href: "/articles/what-is-ml" },
  ]}
/>
```

