# ArticleCard

Article preview for listings and related articles, not article bodies. Uses a full-bleed image, gradient, date, title, author, and CTA.

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `href` | `string` | Required | Full article destination |
| `title` | `string` | Required | Article title |
| `image` | `string` | Required | Background image URL |
| `description` | `string` | — | Short excerpt |
| `imageAlt` | `string` | `title` | Meaningful image alt text |
| `date` | `string` | — | Formatted date |
| `datetime` | `string` | — | ISO date for `<time>` |
| `author` | `Author` | — | Name and avatar |
| `ctaText` | `string` | `"Read more"` | CTA text; empty hides it |
| `className` | `string` | — | Additional CSS classes |
| `variant` | `"default" \| "compact"` | `"default"` | Card size |

## Semantic Hints

`card`, `article-card`, `preview`, `teaser`, `post-card`, `blog-card`, `article-preview`, `content-card`

## Structure and Styling

A single React Router `Link` contains the full-bleed image, bottom-to-top gradient, and bottom-positioned content: date, title, excerpt, author, CTA. Use a consistent 16:9 ratio, bold title, sufficient text contrast, and subtle hover scaling. Compact reduces padding and title size. The CTA is not a nested button. Use `dateTime` in JSX for the HTML `datetime` attribute.

## Implementation — `app/articles/ArticleCard.tsx`

Tailwind utilities below are component-specific choices, not inferred project tokens. No `"use client"` directive is needed: this component uses no browser-only APIs.

```tsx
import { Link } from "react-router";

type Author = {
  name: string;
  avatar: string;
};

type ArticleCardProps = {
  href: string;
  title: string;
  image: string;
  description?: string;
  imageAlt?: string;
  date?: string;
  datetime?: string;
  author?: Author;
  ctaText?: string;
  className?: string;
  variant?: "default" | "compact";
};

export function ArticleCard({
  href,
  title,
  image,
  description,
  imageAlt = title,
  date,
  datetime,
  author,
  ctaText = "Read more",
  className = "",
  variant = "default",
}: ArticleCardProps) {
  const compact = variant === "compact";

  return (
    <Link
      to={href}
      className={`relative flex aspect-video items-end overflow-hidden rounded-lg text-white transition-transform hover:scale-[1.02] focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 ${className}`}
    >
      <img
        src={image}
        alt={imageAlt}
        className="absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover"
      />
      <span className="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-t from-black via-black/70 to-transparent" aria-hidden="true" />
      <div className={`relative ${compact ? "p-3" : "p-6"}`}>
        {date && <time dateTime={datetime}>{date}</time>}
        <h2 className={`font-bold ${compact ? "text-lg" : "text-2xl"}`}>{title}</h2>
        {description && <p>{description}</p>}
        {author && (
          <div className="flex items-center gap-2">
            <img src={author.avatar} alt="" className="h-8 w-8 rounded-full" />
            <span>{author.name}</span>
          </div>
        )}
        {ctaText && <span className="underline">{ctaText}</span>}
      </div>
    </Link>
  );
}
```

## Usage

Render inside the application's React Router context:

```tsx
<ArticleCard
  href="/articles/machine-learning-basics"
  title="Getting Started with Machine Learning"
  image="/images/ml-basics.jpg"
  date="January 15, 2024"
  datetime="2024-01-15"
  author={{
    name: "Jane Smith",
    avatar: "/avatars/jane.jpg",
  }}
/>
```

