# ArticleResourceDownload

Resource CTA for PDFs, templates, and guides. Place mid-article after establishing value.

## Props

| Prop | Type | Default | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `topic` | `string` | Required | Topic used in the default title |
| `title` | `string` | `${topic} Checklist & Notes` | Custom title |
| `description` | `string` | See code | Custom description |
| `buttonLabel` | `string` | `"Download Checklist (PDF)"` | Download link text |
| `buttonHref` | `string` | `"#"` | Resource URL; supply a real URL in production |
| `eyebrow` | `string` | `"Free download"` | Text above title |
| `className` | `string` | — | Additional container classes |
| `previewImages` | `string[]` | — | Preview URLs; first two are displayed |

## Semantic hints

`resource-cta`, `download-cta`, `pdf-cta`, `guide-cta`, `lead-magnet`, `gated-content`, `resource-download`

## Implementation — `app/articles/ArticleResourceDownload.tsx`

Use React Router’s `Link` with `reloadDocument` so resource requests bypass client-side routing. `download` is a browser hint; cross-origin downloads depend on server headers. No client directive is needed.

```tsx
import type { ReactElement } from "react";
import { Link } from "react-router";

type ArticleResourceDownloadProps = {
  topic: string;
  title?: string;
  description?: string;
  buttonLabel?: string;
  buttonHref?: string;
  eyebrow?: string;
  className?: string;
  previewImages?: string[];
};

export function ArticleResourceDownload({
  topic,
  title = `${topic} Checklist & Notes`,
  description = "Download a practical checklist and notes for your next project.",
  buttonLabel = "Download Checklist (PDF)",
  buttonHref = "#",
  eyebrow = "Free download",
  className = "",
  previewImages = [],
}: ArticleResourceDownloadProps): ReactElement {
  return (
    <div
      data-cf-resource-download
      className={`relative isolate overflow-hidden rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-br from-indigo-50 to-white p-8 ${className}`}
    >
      <div
        aria-hidden="true"
        className="pointer-events-none absolute -right-12 -top-12 -z-10 h-64 w-64 rounded-full bg-indigo-200 blur-3xl"
      />
      <div className="grid items-center gap-8 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <span className="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-indigo-800">
            {eyebrow}
          </span>
          <h3 className="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold text-slate-950">{title}</h3>
          <p className="mt-4 max-w-prose text-slate-700">{description}</p>
          <Link
            to={buttonHref}
            reloadDocument
            download
            className="mt-6 inline-block rounded-lg bg-indigo-700 px-5 py-3 font-semibold text-white shadow-lg hover:bg-indigo-800 motion-safe:transition-transform motion-safe:hover:scale-105 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-4 focus-visible:outline-indigo-700"
          >
            {buttonLabel}
          </Link>
        </div>
        <div aria-hidden="true" className="flex justify-center gap-3">
          {[0, 1].map((index) => (
            <div
              key={index}
              className={`w-40 rounded-lg bg-white p-3 shadow-xl motion-safe:transition-transform motion-safe:hover:rotate-0 motion-safe:hover:scale-105 ${index === 0 ? "-rotate-3" : "translate-y-4 rotate-3"}`}
            >
              {previewImages[index] ? (
                <img src={previewImages[index]} alt="" className="w-full" />
              ) : (
                <div className="h-48 bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-200 to-white" />
              )}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Route usage

Render inside an existing React Router route:

```tsx
<ArticleResourceDownload
  topic="Machine Learning"
  title="Complete ML Project Checklist"
  buttonHref="/downloads/ml-checklist.pdf"
  previewImages={[
    "/previews/ml-page1.png",
    "/previews/ml-page2.png",
  ]}
/>
```

